  "why": "a postponed game passes the counted-game rule, reports state 'post' with completed false, and carries scores '0' and '0'. So: never key 'finished' off state=='post', and never read a score before completed -- 0-0 is a tie, which the NBA cannot produce. Every season carries a few: 2 in 2023-24, 5 in 2024-25, 4 in 2025-26, which is why the counted-game rule yields 1,232-1,235 and only the DECIDED subset is 1,230 games / 30 teams / 82 each."
